  <!-- ===================================================================
       TASK 1b — "WHAT MAKES A GOOD WRITER?"  (drag-to-rank; 3 sets, ONE PER
       SCREEN). Each set is its own screen; the chat reveals the next set only
       after the previous CapaProblem is submitted (wait @<grader>.submitCount).
       Submit button relabeled via submitLabel="Submit". The three inputs
       (wj2_good_1/2/3) keep their ids so the results tool still reads them, and each
       ranked item carries its own semantic id: SortableInput stores the arrangement as
       indices into source order, but the item ids are what buildArrangementWithPositions
       keys on (and what shows up in the event stream), so they must not be auto-generated
       hashes of the prose. The prompt's index legend below names them alongside the index.
       =================================================================== -->

  <Vertical id="wj2_good_1_screen">
    <Markdown>
## 🏆 The Quiz — Part 2: What Makes a Good Writer?

**Set 1 of 3**  `█░░`

Trust your gut — there are no right or wrong answers here, since these are genuinely a matter of
opinion. Being honest gives you the most accurate writing profile.
    </Markdown>
    <CapaProblem id="wj2_good_1_problem" title="What makes a good writer? (Set 1)" showanswer="never" submitLabel="Submit">
      <Markdown>Drag to rank from **most important** (top) to **least important** (bottom), then press Submit:</Markdown>
      <SortableGrader id="wj2_good_1_grader" algorithm="survey">
        <SortableInput id="wj2_good_1" dragMode="whole">
          <Markdown id="wj2_good_1_understand_assignment"> Taking the time to understand an assignment before starting to write. </Markdown>
          <Markdown id="wj2_good_1_express_accurately"   > Expressing one's ideas accurately.                                 </Markdown>
          <Markdown id="wj2_good_1_long_enough"          > Making sure to write something that is long enough for the task.   </Markdown>
          <Markdown id="wj2_good_1_finish_quickly"       > Finishing writing tasks quickly.                                   </Markdown>
        </SortableInput>
      </SortableGrader>
    </CapaProblem>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="wj2_good_2_screen">
    <Markdown>
## 🏆 The Quiz — Part 2: What Makes a Good Writer?

**Set 2 of 3**  `██░`

Trust your gut — there are no right or wrong answers here, since these are genuinely a matter of
opinion. Being honest gives you the most accurate writing profile.
    </Markdown>
